- JavaScript bundle size
- Unused JavaScript
- Render-blocking resources
- Image dimensions and formats
- Font loading
- Lazy loading
- Caching
- Compression
- Network requests
- Third-party scripts
- Layout shifts
- Mobile responsiveness

Use the following Core Web Vitals targets as reference thresholds, assessed at the 75th percentile when real-user data is available:

- LCP: 2.5 seconds or less
- INP: 200 milliseconds or less
- CLS: 0.1 or less

Do not confuse laboratory measurements with real-user field data.

### Optimization tasks

Where justified:

- Convert oversized images to modern formats.
- Add appropriate image dimensions.
- Use responsive images.
- Lazy-load below-the-fold images.
- Do not lazy-load the primary above-the-fold image unnecessarily.
- Optimize font loading.
- Reduce unnecessary JavaScript.
- Remove genuinely unused dependencies only after checking their usage.
- Split bundles where useful.
- Avoid layout shifts.
- Improve caching and compression using compatible hosting configuration.
- Reduce expensive rendering and unnecessary animations.

Preserve the existing design and functionality.

